    [Compared @pdf:pl of the execution time between status quo and refactored code for use case 2. The x-axis represents average time in ms, while the y-axis represents the density. The red and blue distributions belong to the status quo and refactored code, respectively. Each distribution's mean execution time is displayed in the plot. The distribution of the status quo code is more concentrated, with a significantly higher peak that lies left of the refactored code's lower peak. The refactoring's distribution is much flatter and stretched out.],
    [Use Case 2 - Compared execution time distribution of status quo & refactoring]
  )
) <results2-plot>

#figure(
  table(
    columns: 3,
    [Metric], [Estimate], [95% confidence interval],
    [Mean], [8.769 µs], [\[8.739 µs, 8.802 µs\]],
    [Std. Dev.], [161.20 ns], [\[130.17 ns, 186.87 ns\]],
    [Change in time], [+1.252%], [\[+0.905%, +1.653%\]],
